<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · ideology</p><h1 class="enc-title">Social democracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1844">1844 CE</a> – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Social democracy is a centre-left ideology that seeks social equality through gradual, democratic reform within a regulated, mostly capitalist economy. Born in the 19th-century labour movement, it parted from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a> after 1917 and built the welfare states of post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>; since the 1970s it has contended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neoliberalism">neoliberalism</a>, the Third Way and electoral decline.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…as a kingdom that grew from the Svear and Geats into the dominant Baltic power of the seventeenth century, shaping the Thirty Years’ War and the eastern Baltic, and then remade itself through neutrality, industrialisation and <b>social democracy</b> into one of the world’s most prosperous and stable states.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The ulama sought to extend their own power and to have Shi'i Islam more strictly enforced; the liberals and radicals wanted greater political and <b>social democracy</b> and economic development; and the bazaaris wanted to restrict the favoured economic status of foreigners and their competition.</blockquote><a href="/movement/persian-constitutional-revolution">Persian Constitutional Revolution · Aims</a></li><li><blockquote>Commentators have noted the closeness of social liberalism to <b>social democracy</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/liberalism">Liberalism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>By the early 1920s communism and <b>social democracy</b> were the two dominant tendencies of the movement.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/socialism">Socialism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>It peaked before and after the First World War and in Spain in 1936, then declined under repression and the rise of communism and <b>social democracy</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/syndicalism">Syndicalism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>Between 1975 and 1991 the MPLA ran a Marxist-Leninist one-party state, then in 1990 declared <b>social democracy</b> its platform.</blockquote><a href="/state/angola">Angola</a></li></ul></section>
